ince you you went over you can  ask a question or two if you like okay  because i know that someone's gonna  answer differently than some other  people have but i would like to ask the  exact same question this panel  you know have you heard of anything have  you seen anything have you read anything  that in any way justifies the murder of  those four atf agents by david question  as followers  and the wounding of 20 more and  or absolves david koresh  from the guilt of having those 80 people  die  with  mr quintin  no sir not in my opinion mr gray  me neither mr chair  mr dora i don't believe they were  murdered i think they were set at risks  by their own agencies going ahead  knowing that we in all likelihood knew  they were coming  i think that they went against their own  laws  attacking a building no knowing that  there were women and children in there  if the officers exposed themselves to  fire by stepping out and emptying their  magazines into the building and someone  did shoot them  uh i would consider that self-defense  not murder  i don't think anybody is justified in  doing murder defending yourself is a  different proposition and we don't call  it murder if we go and shoot people in a  wartime situation and that certainly  looked like a battle to us  you had one follow-up and i will permit  it  i really do appreciate that but mr joy  david koresh would not have been able to  physically to escape because of his  wounds  but he his body was found  with a bullet hole  through his mouth  and the barrel of a gun lying next to  him not the belt the yes  and  uh which would certainly have indicated  that david koresh and others did indeed  commit suicide what what is your thought  about that  i am not aware that he had a bullet hole  in his mouth i understand he had a  bullet hole in the head all right now  whether somebody else shot him i don't  know apparently you know it's possible  um  i can only tell you what i was told it's  hearsay  rennes abraham told me he was sitting in  the hall upstairs  and uh  at one point in the in the morning and  he went into the front room which he  ended up exiting from  retirement renis abraham went into this  room that he ended up exiting from and  in the room he said was david koresh  steve schneider and mark wendell he said  they were sitting on a bed talking  he says and he went in and was listening  to what they were having to say he said  the next thing the room filled with  smoke  he says and he walked over to the window  and trying to get a breath of fresh air  and he said the thought came to him why  am i standing here sucking air through a  broken window why don't i just go out so  he went out on the on the roof  and that was as i say the last time that  he saw david uh both steve schneider and  david have bullet  now whether  somebody shot them to put them out of  their misery whether they ran out into  the hall and found they were in the  middle of the fire instead of escaping  it i don't know i don't know what they  went through because i wasn't there  i  figured that if somebody did  what found themselves trapped and was  were burning and suffering if they asked  for somebody to put them out of the  misery i wouldn't condemn that person  but i don't know the i never there was  no one in our area that came up with  bullet holes thank the lord and uh  so there was no condemnation in that  area for us that escaped  but i couldn't speak for the others  thank you mr slaughter well we we've  certainly been a long day today i want  to thank all of you for being here in  this panel i know miss joy has been  particularly tough on you but we want to  thank the professionals are here for  helping us walk through this fire it has  been one of the great uh i guess  discussed  parts of the entire waco affair and i  hope that after this we can assess  better with your help what happened on  that final fateful day we will be in  recess until monday morning at 10 a.m we  will reconvene